i.gz\ninput/data/sub-063_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-067_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-069_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-071_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-073_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-075_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-077_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-079_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-081_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-083_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-085_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-087_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-089_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-093_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-095_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-099_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-103_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-105_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-107_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-109_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-113_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-115_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-117_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-119_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-121_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/data/sub-123_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\ninput/participants.tsv\ninput/sources.json\ninput/study-task.md\ninput/upstream-methods.md\nprotocol.md\nREADME.md\nreport\nreport/analysis-report.md\nresources\nresources/nilearn\nresources/nilearn/fsl\nresources/nilearn/README.md\nresults\nresults/analysis_log.txt\nresults/analysis_mask.nii.gz\nresults/max_t_null.npy\nresults/mean_effect.nii.gz\nresults/p_fwe_positive.nii.gz\nresults/participant_qc.tsv\nresults/replay-check.txt\nresults/run_history.md\nresults/significant_fwe_mask.nii.gz\nresults/summary.json\nresults/t_positive.nii.gz\nresults/vmPFC_participant_estimates.tsv\n?? README.md\n?? analysis/\n?? figures/\n?? protocol.md\n?? report/\n?? resources/\n?? results/\n!! .codex/\n!! .entire/\ne929d62 chore(study): supply materialized scientific inputs\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: run_probes.py [-h] [-o OUTPUT] [--response RESPONSE]\n                     [--only {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]]\n                     [--skip {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]]\n                     [--check-remote] [--allow GLOB [GLOB ...]]\n                     [--kind {dataset,component,study,skill}] [--overwrite]\n                     [--quiet]\n                     path\n\nRun the STAMPED probes over a checked-out research object.\n\n    run_probes.py <path> [-o probes.json] [--response response.json]\n                  [--only NAME ...] [--skip NAME ...] [--check-remote]\n                  [--kind dataset|component|study|skill]\n\nWrites the per-probe results, and optionally a response JSON (the format in\n``../stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md``) in which every item a\nprobe speaks to carries that probe's verdict and every other item is left\n``not-checked`` for the assessing session to judge.\nWithout a Git commit, ``-o`` retains a limitation receipt and exit code 2;\nno response draft is produced.\n\nThe probes never modify the object.  Nothing here replaces the judgement items:\na response straight out of this script is a draft, not an assessment.\n\npositional arguments:\n  path                  checked-out object to probe\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -o, --output OUTPUT   write the probe results here\n  --response RESPONSE   also write a draft response JSON here\n  --only {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]\n                        run just these probes\n  --skip {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]\n  --check-remote        contact submodule urls (network)\n  --allow GLOB [GLOB ...]\n                        paths no-abs-paths may skip, for files that genuinely\n                        have to carry a host path\n  --kind {dataset,component,study,skill}\n  --overwrite           replace an existing --response file instead of keeping\n                        its judged answers\n  --quiet\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py [-h]\n                          {items,validate,encode,decode,template,set,stamp,table} ...\n\nSTAMPED checklist responses: read the items, validate, encode, decode.\n\nThe vendored checklist in ``../checklist/`` is the only item source, and this\nscript is the only writer of a checklist-app URL.  See\n``../references/response-format.md`` for the response JSON and\n``../references/verdicts.md`` for the statuses.\n\nSubcommands\n-----------\nitems      list the pinned items (id, level, principle codes, text)\nset        answer one item in a response JSON, in place (what every run was\n           otherwise writing a merge script for)\ntable      the per-item markdown table response-format.md section 4 asks for\nstamp      fill harness, model, scope and kind; optionally hash a retained capture\nvalidate   check a response JSON against the pin and the app's constraints\nencode     response JSON -> checklist-app URL\ndecode     checklist-app URL -> response JSON (how a filled web form becomes\n           reference answers for calibration)\ntemplate   emit a response JSON skeleton with every item not-checked\n\nExit codes: 0 ok, 1 validation failed, 2 usage.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {items,validate,encode,decode,template,set,stamp,table}\n    items               list the pinned items\n    validate            check a response JSON\n    encode              response JSON -> URL\n    decode              URL -> response JSON\n    template            emit an all-not-checked response JSON\n    set                 answer one item in a response JSON, in place\n    stamp               fill harness, model, scope, kind and capture identity\n    table               print the per-item markdown table\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -o probes.json >commands/probes.stdout 2>commands/probes.stderr; status=$?; printf '\"'exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$status\" >commands/probes.exit; cat commands/probes.stdout; cat commands/probes.stderr; exit 0'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -o probes.json >commands/probes.stdout 2>commands/probes.stderr; status=$?; printf '\"'exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$status\" >commands/probes.exit; cat commands/probes.stdout; cat commands/probes.stderr; exit 0'","aggregated_output":"probe                    status          items\nci-present               not-checked     should/002, should/006\nclone-weight             met             (extra)\nderived-have-records     not-applicable  must/006\nentry-point              unmet           must/007, must/008\nenv-spec-tracked         unmet           must/010, must/013, must/016\ninputs-untouched         not-applicable  (extra)\nlarge-in-annex           met             must/005\nlicense-declared         unmet           (extra)\nmodules-separated        partial         should/003\nno-abs-paths             met             must/009\nplatform-assumptions     not-checked     must/011, must/012\nrun-env-linked           not-checked     must/006, must/015\nsubdatasets-resolvable   not-checked     must/002, may/001\ntree-clean               unmet           must/004\n\nprobes cover 13/17 MUST items; inspect statuses for completed verdicts\n\nwrote probes.json\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'for f in README.md protocol.md report/analysis-report.md input/study-task.md input/upstream-methods.md analysis/group_analysis.py input/participants.tsv results/summary.json results/analysis_log.txt results/run_history.md results/replay-check.txt; do echo \"===== $f\"; sed -n '\"'1,260p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/$f\"; done; echo '\"'===== top-level'; find \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -maxdepth 1 -type f -print -exec ls -l {} '\"\\\\;\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'for f in README.md protocol.md report/analysis-report.md input/study-task.md input/upstream-methods.md analysis/group_analysis.py input/participants.tsv results/summary.json results/analysis_log.txt results/run_history.md results/replay-check.txt; do echo \"===== $f\"; sed -n '\"'1,260p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/$f\"; done; echo '\"'===== top-level'; find \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -maxdepth 1 -type f -print -exec ls -l {} '\"\\\\;\"","aggregated_output":"===== README.md\n# NARPS potential gain group analysis\n\nConcise report: [`report/analysis-report.md`](report/analysis-report.md)\n\nReplay the group analysis from the workspace root with:\n\n```sh\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/group_analysis.py\n```\n\nThe analysis uses only the supplied participant gain-effect maps and metadata; see [`protocol.md`](protocol.md) for the recorded group-analysis decisions. Results and editable analysis source are provided in `results/`, `analysis/` and `figures/`.\n===== protocol.md\n# Analysis protocol\n\n## Question and estimand\n\nTest whether the mean participant gain-effect estimate is greater than zero in the equal-indifference cohort (N=54). The supplied contrast maps are participant-level parameter estimates for a mean-centered, variance-normalized gain modulator. The estimand is therefore the cohort mean of those contrast estimates, not change in BOLD per currency unit.\n\n## Data and unit\n\nUse all 54 `input/data/*_hypo1_cope.nii.gz` images identified in `input/sources.json`, joined one-to-one by participant ID to `input/participants.tsv`. The independent sampling unit is participant. Do not repeat upstream preprocessing or individual modeling. Check file hashes, dimensions, affine, finiteness, coverage and metadata join before group analysis. Exclude only an input that fails a declared integrity/spatial/QC check; record any exclusion and reason.\n\n## Model and inference\n\nPrimary model: one-sample group mean at each voxel, testing positive mean (one-sided, ex ante directional hypothesis). Estimate uncertainty across participants. Use sign-flip permutation of participant maps with a maximum-t statistic across the complete analysis mask for family-wise error control over the whole brain. Use 9,999 random sign patterns plus the observed arrangement; fix and record the seed and use the plus-one permutation p-value. This inference assumes participant effects are independent and sign-exchangeable under the null. Also report conventional one-sample t estimates and uncorrected p-values as descriptive support, not as the hypothesis decision.\n\nThe analysis mask is the common spatial support of all input maps (nonzero finite values in every participant), because zero-filled voxels outside the upstream brain analysis mask are not observations. Document voxel count and geometry. Operationalize vmPFC with a literature-defined 5 mm MNI sphere centered at [2, 46, -8], reported as a vmPFC valuation focus in Bartra et al. (2013), external to these maps. The localization supports the claim only if a positive whole-brain FWE-significant voxel is within that independently defined ROI. Report ROI summaries descriptively and do not use them to replace whole-brain correction.\n\n## QC, uncertainty and limitations\n\nRetain a participant QC table and descriptive maps/distributions. Report N and exclusions, sign-flip count, mask, peak coordinates, effect estimate and uncertainty, FWE p-value, and whether any corrected voxel intersects the vmPFC ROI. Report a sensitivity check against an independent one-sample t implementation. Note that participant variance maps and upstream model are unavailable; group inference treats contrast maps as measured effects and cannot propagate first-level uncertainty. The upstream gain regressor normalization prevents interpreting coefficients per currency unit, and gain and loss were modeled separately.\n\n## Deliverables and stopping rule\n\nProvide executable analysis code, machine-readable results, figures, a concise report, and a documented command/environment. Stop after data/QC review, primary inference, independent numerical check, figure inspection, and replay of the recorded analysis.\n===== report/analysis-report.md\n# Potential gains and vmPFC activity\n\n## Result\n\n**The supplied group maps do not support a greater vmPFC response with increasing potential gain.** Across the 54 equal-indifference participants, the mean estimate in an independent 5 mm vmPFC sphere centered at MNI [2, 46, −8] was −0.012 upstream regressor units (95% t interval −0.052 to 0.028; one-sample t(53) = −0.60, one-sided p = .726). No positive voxel in the sphere survived the prespecified whole-brain family-wise error (FWE) correction.\n\nThe positive, whole-brain one-sided max-t test did identify 24 FWE-significant voxels elsewhere (smallest corrected p = .0006; peak at MNI [−26, −102, −3.6], mean estimate 0.112, t(53) = 6.62). This posterior finding does not localize to vmPFC and does not establish the hypothesized vmPFC effect. The tested hypothesis was directional and the family-wise correction covered the complete common map support (198,029 voxels), consistent with the original NARPS instruction to test a positive gain effect in vmPFC for the equal-indifference group ([original instructions, Hypothesis 1](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf)).\n\n![Participant estimates in the independent vmPFC sphere](../figures/vmPFC_roi_estimates.png)\n\n![Positive whole-brain FWE-significant effects](../figures/wholebrain_fwe.png)\n\n## Data and analysis\n\nThe analysis used all 54 source-listed AO86 participant gain-effect maps and their matching metadata rows. Maps are in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space at 2 × 2 × 2.4 mm. SHA-256 checks, one-to-one participant IDs, dimensions, affine, and finite values passed; there were no exclusions. The analysis mask was the intersection of finite, nonzero support across all maps, excluding zero-filled outside-mask voxels. The unit of analysis was participant.\n\nFor each voxel, we estimated the mean participant effect and tested whether it was positive using a one-sample t statistic. Family-wise error was controlled with 9,999 random participant sign-flips and the maximum positive t statistic over the entire mask (seed 20261016; plus-one permutation p-values; α = .05). Sign-flipping assumes participant effects are independent and exchangeable in sign under the null. The max observed statistic and independent SciPy one-sample t-test agreed exactly (t = 6.617173 at the selected peak); the custom signed-t formula also matched SciPy for three fixed sign patterns. The vmPFC sphere was set independently from published valuation literature ([Bartra, McGuire & Kable, 2013](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2013.02.063)); the 5 mm radius is an operational spatial definition, since vmPFC has no single universally agreed atlas boundary. The parametric ROI interval and p-value are descriptive and uncorrected; the whole-brain FWE test is the primary hypothesis decision.\n\n## Interpretation and limits\n\nThe ROI interval includes zero and is compatible with modest positive or negative group means; failure to find a corrected voxel is not evidence that the response is exactly zero or that no participant has a positive response. The study has 54 participants and this group-level analysis does not propagate first-level uncertainty because participant variance maps were not supplied. The maps are effect estimates, not standardized statistics. Their gain modulator was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution, so estimates cannot be interpreted as BOLD change per currency unit or as a response slope for a fixed dollar increment. The upstream model, including the separate gain and loss models, is fixed; this analysis neither revisits that model nor tests gain against loss. Accordingly, the result is a lack of whole-brain-corrected group evidence for the specified vmPFC hypothesis under the supplied upstream model, rather than a definitive null or causal claim.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nFrom the workspace root, run:\n\n```sh\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/group_analysis.py\n```\n\nThe script writes the tables, NIfTI maps, permutation null distribution, summary JSON and figures beneath `results/` and `figures/`. It uses Python 3.13.16, NumPy 2.5.4, SciPy 1.18.1, NiBabel 5.4.2, Nilearn 0.14.1, pandas 3.0.6 and Matplotlib 3.11.2. Input image byte hashes and software versions are recorded in [`results/summary.json`](../results/summary.json); participant QC is in [`results/participant_qc.tsv`](../results/participant_qc.tsv). The finalized command was replayed and selected scientific outputs matched byte-for-byte ([digest comparison](../results/replay-check.txt)); run history is in [`results/run_history.md`](../results/run_history.md). Analysis protocol: [`protocol.md`](../protocol.md).\n===== input/study-task.md\n# Potential gains and brain activity\n\nDoes increasing potential monetary gain produce a greater fMRI response in the ventromedial prefrontal cortex (vmPFC) in the NARPS equal-indifference group?\n\nTest the hypothesis that this response increases with potential gain.\nParticipants performed a mixed-gambles task, deciding whether to accept gambles with possible gains and losses.\nIn this group, the range of potential gains was twice the range of potential losses.\n\nInvestigate the question at the group-analysis stage using the supplied 54 participant gain-effect maps and metadata.\nPreprocessing and individual modeling are fixed inputs, described in `upstream-methods.md`; do not repeat them or download time-series scans.\nChoose scientifically defensible group models, quality checks, software and visualizations.\nAccount for what the supplied effect estimates measure and the limits of their upstream model.\nUse whole-brain correction for multiple comparisons when evaluating support for the hypothesis, as required by the original study; justify how you identify vmPFC.\n\nProduce a concise scientific report with informative figures and the code and results supporting your conclusions.\nExplain uncertainty, exclusions and limitations, including what a lack of support would mean.\nPrior teams' answers are not ground truth or a required result.\n\nSource: [NARPS original analysis instructions, Hypothesis 1](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf).\n===== input/upstream-methods.md\n# Fixed upstream analysis\n\nEach map is one participant's unthresholded gain-effect estimate from NARPS team AO86, averaged across four runs.\nThe 54 participants comprise the complete equal-indifference group in OpenNeuro ds001734 version 1.0.4.\nThese are effect estimates, not standardized test statistics or group results.\nMaps are reported in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space.\n\nAO86 used fMRIPrep outputs and nistats participant models.\nTheir reported gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution; its coefficients must not be interpreted as change per currency unit.\nResponse trials used response-time durations, with separate response-choice and gain modulators.\nNonresponse trials, motion terms, flagged volumes and drift terms were also modeled; runs were combined within participant.\nGain and loss used separate models, so the supplied gain effect is conditional on that modeling choice.\n\nThe reported upstream choices are fixed for this task.\nParticipant variance maps and a complete executable upstream pipeline are not supplied; account for these limits when choosing and interpreting group inference.\n`participants.tsv` retains the source group, age and gender columns.\n`sources.json` identifies each original image, its retrieved-byte checksum, the pinned cohort table and the original methods report.\n===== analysis/group_analysis.py\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"One-sample group inference on supplied NARPS AO86 participant effect maps.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport hashlib, json, os, platform, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nos.environ.setdefault(\"MPLBACKEND\", \"Agg\")\nos.environ.setdefault(\"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\", \"1\")\nos.environ.setdefault(\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\", \"1\")\nimport nibabel as nib\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport scipy\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom nilearn import plotting\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nINPUT = ROOT / \"input\"\nOUT = ROOT / \"results\"\nFIG = ROOT / \"figures\"\nSEED = 20261016\nN_PERM = 9999\nALPHA = 0.05\n\n\ndef sha256(path):\n    h=hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(path,'rb') as f:\n        for block in iter(lambda:f.read(1024*1024),b''): h.update(block)\n    return h.hexdigest()\n\n\ndef main():\n    meta=json.loads((INPUT/'sources.json').read_text())\n    participants=pd.read_csv(INPUT/'participants.tsv',sep='\\t')\n    if participants.participant_id.duplicated().any(): raise ValueError('duplicate participant IDs')\n    if len(participants)!=54 or set(participants.group)!={'equalIndifference'}: raise ValueError('unexpected cohort')\n    paths=[]; rows=[]\n    for pid in participants.participant_id:\n        rel=f'data/{pid}_hypo1_cope.nii.gz'\n        p=INPUT/rel\n        if not p.exists(): raise FileNotFoundError(p)\n        if sha256(p)!=meta['files'][rel]['sha256']: raise ValueError(f'hash mismatch {pid}')\n        im=nib.load(str(p)); arr=im.get_fdata(dtype=np.float32)\n        if len(im.shape)!=3 or not np.isfinite(arr).all(): raise ValueError(f'invalid image {pid}')\n        if paths and (im.shape!=ref.shape or not np.allclose(im.affine,ref.affine,atol=1e-5)): raise ValueError('image geometry mismatch')\n        if not paths: ref=im\n        paths.append(p)\n        rows.append({'participant_id':pid,'group':participants.set_index('participant_id').loc[pid,'group'],\n                     'age':participants.set_index('participant_id').loc[pid,'age'],\n                     'gender':participants.set_index('participant_id').loc[pid,'gender'],\n                     'sha256':sha256(p),'finite_voxels':int(np.isfinite(arr).sum()),\n                     'nonzero_voxels':int(np.count_nonzero(arr)), 'map_mean_all_voxels':float(arr.mean()),\n                     'map_sd_all_voxels':float(arr.std()),'map_min':float(arr.min()),'map_max':float(arr.max())})\n    # Zero-filled voxels outside the common upstream analysis support are not observations.\n    stack=np.stack([nib.load(str(p)).get_fdata(dtype=np.float32) for p in paths],axis=0)\n    mask=np.all(np.isfinite(stack)&(stack!=0),axis=0)\n    if not mask.any(): raise ValueError('empty common support')\n    X=stack[:,mask].astype(np.float64)\n    n, v=X.shape\n    # Independent, two-sided descriptive t statistics; primary direction is positive.\n    mean=X.mean(axis=0); sd=X.std(axis=0,ddof=1)\n    t_obs=mean/(sd/np.sqrt(n))\n    p_unc=stats.t.sf(t_obs,n-1)\n    # Independent literature-defined vmPFC ROI: 5 mm sphere, MNI [2, 46, -8].\n    # This reported vmPFC locus is external to the present maps (Bartra et al. 2013).\n    ijk=np.indices(ref.shape).reshape(3,-1).T\n    xyz=nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine,ijk)\n    roi_full=(np.linalg.norm(xyz-np.array([2.,46.,-8.]),axis=1)<=5.).reshape(ref.shape)\n    roi=roi_full&mask\n    if roi.sum()==0: raise ValueError('vmPFC anatomical proxy has no overlap with analysis mask')\n    # Primary max-t sign-flip correction, positive one-sided familywise inference.\n    rng=np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n    max_null=np.empty(N_PERM,dtype=np.float64)\n    # Batched multiplication limits memory while preserving exact studentized statistic.\n    batch=100\n    for start in range(0,N_PERM,batch):\n        b=min(batch,N_PERM-start)\n        signs=rng.choice(np.array([-1.,1.]),size=(b,n))\n        sums=signs@X\n        ss=np.sum(X*X,axis=0)[None,:]\n        denom=np.sqrt(np.maximum(n*ss-sums*sums,0))\n        # Exact one-sample t under participant sign flips.\n        tperm=np.divide(sums*np.sqrt(n-1),denom,out=np.zeros_like(sums),where=denom>0)\n        max_null[start:start+b]=np.max(tperm,axis=1)\n    p_fwe=(1+np.sum(max_null[:,None]>=t_obs[None,:],axis=0))/(N_PERM+1)\n    sig=(p_fwe<=ALPHA)&(t_obs>0)\n    sig_vol=np.zeros(ref.shape,dtype=bool); sig_vol[mask]=sig\n    # Confidence interval for descriptive ROI mean, with participant as sampling unit.\n    roi_data=stack[:,roi]\n    roi_sub=roi_data.mean(axis=1)\n    roi_mean=float(roi_sub.mean()); roi_sd=float(roi_sub.std(ddof=1)); roi_se=roi_sd/np.sqrt(n)\n    roi_ci=stats.t.interval(0.95,n-1,loc=roi_mean,scale=roi_se)\n    roi_t,roi_p2=stats.ttest_1samp(roi_sub,0)\n    roi_p1=float(stats.t.sf(roi_t,n-1))\n    # Independent numerical check: compare one randomly selected voxel against scipy's one-sample t-test.\n    check_idx=int(np.argmax(t_obs))\n    check=stats.ttest_1samp(X[:,check_idx],0,alternative='greater')\n    if not np.isclose(check.statistic,t_obs[check_idx],rtol=1e-10,atol=1e-10): raise AssertionError('SciPy t check failed')\n    # Validate custom sign-flip studentization against SciPy for fixed patterns.\n    sign_checks=np.vstack([np.ones(n),np.where(np.arange(n)%2,1.,-1.),rng.choice(np.array([-1.,1.]),size=n)])\n    perm_formula=[]; perm_scipy=[]\n    for s in sign_checks:\n        sv=s@X[:,check_idx]\n        denom_check=np.sqrt(max(n*np.sum(X[:,check_idx]**2)-sv**2,0))\n        perm_formula.append(sv*np.sqrt(n-1)/denom_check)\n        perm_scipy.append(float(stats.ttest_1samp(X[:,check_idx]*s,0).statistic))\n    if not np.allclose(perm_formula,perm_scipy,rtol=1e-10,atol=1e-10): raise AssertionError('SciPy sign-flip check failed')\n    # save analysis mask and image-space group estimates\n    def save_vol(values,name,dtype=np.float32):\n        vol=np.zeros(ref.shape,dtype=dtype); vol[mask]=values\n        out=nib.Nifti1Image(vol,ref.affine,ref.header); out.set_data_dtype(dtype); nib.save(out,str(OUT/name))\n    save_vol(mean,'mean_effect.nii.gz')\n    save_vol(t_obs,'t_positive.nii.gz')\n    save_vol(p_fwe,'p_fwe_positive.nii.gz')\n    save_vol(sig.astype(np.uint8),'significant_fwe_mask.nii.gz',np.uint8)\n    nib.save(nib.Nifti1Image(mask.astype(np.uint8),ref.affine,ref.header),str(OUT/'analysis_mask.nii.gz'))\n    # compact tables and machine-readable summary\n    pd.DataFrame(rows).to_csv(OUT/'participant_qc.tsv',sep='\\t',index=False)\n    pd.DataFrame({'participant_id':participants.participant_id,'vmPFC_proxy_mean_effect':roi_sub}).to_csv(OUT/'vmPFC_participant_estimates.tsv',sep='\\t',index=False)\n    peak=None\n    if sig.any():\n        inds=np.argwhere(mask)\n        # voxel with smallest corrected p among discoveries\n        candidates=np.flatnonzero(sig); k=candidates[np.argmin(p_fwe[candidates])]\n        ijk=inds[k]; xyz=nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine,ijk)\n        peak={'ijk':ijk.tolist(),'xyz_mni_mm':[float(a) for a in xyz],\n              'mean_effect_estimate':float(mean[k]),'t':float(t_obs[k]),'p_uncorrected_one_sided':float(p_unc[k]),'p_fwe_one_sided':float(p_fwe[k]),'in_vmPFC_proxy':bool(roi[tuple(ijk)])}\n    summary={'N':n,'exclusions':[],'participant_map_count':len(paths),'analysis_mask_voxels':int(mask.sum()),'map_shape':list(ref.shape),'voxel_sizes_mm':[float(x) for x in ref.header.get_zooms()],\n      'analysis_mask_rule':'finite, nonzero common support across all 54 participant maps',\n      'vmPFC_roi':'Independent literature-defined 5 mm sphere centered MNI [2, 46, -8] (Bartra et al., 2013); sphere clipped to common analysis support.', 'vmPFC_roi_voxels_in_analysis_mask':int(roi.sum()),\n      'primary_test':'one-sample positive group mean; participant sign-flip permutation max-t over common-support voxels', 'permutations':N_PERM,'seed':SEED,'pseudocount':'(1 + number of null maxima >= observed t) / (N_PERM + 1)','alpha_fwe':ALPHA,\n      'positive_fwe_significant_voxels':int(sig.sum()),'any_positive_fwe_discovery_in_vmPFC_proxy':bool(np.any(sig_vol&roi)), 'smallest_fwe_p':float(p_fwe.min()),'peak_discovery':peak,\n      'vmPFC_proxy_mean':roi_mean,'vmPFC_proxy_sd_between_participants':roi_sd,'vmPFC_proxy_95ci_t':[float(roi_ci[0]),float(roi_ci[1])],'vmPFC_proxy_t':float(roi_t),'vmPFC_proxy_p_one_sided_uncorrected':roi_p1,'vmPFC_proxy_p_two_sided_uncorrected':float(roi_p2),\n      'numerical_check':'SciPy one-sample t-test agrees at maximum observed voxel; custom signed-t formula matches SciPy for three fixed sign patterns at the same voxel','max_t_check_voxel_index':check_idx,'max_t_scipy_t':float(check.statistic),'max_t_manual_t':float(t_obs[check_idx]),'sign_flip_check_t_scipy':[float(x) for x in perm_scipy],'sign_flip_check_t_formula':[float(x) for x in perm_formula],\n      'versions':{'python':sys.version.split()[0],'numpy':np.__version__,'scipy':scipy.__version__,'nibabel':nib.__version__,'nilearn':__import__('nilearn').__version__,'pandas':pd.__version__,'platform':platform.platform()},\n      'input_sha256':{str(p.relative_to(ROOT)):sha256(p) for p in paths},'participant_table_sha256':sha256(INPUT/'participants.tsv'),'source_manifest_sha256':sha256(INPUT/'sources.json')}\n    (OUT/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2)+'\\n')\n    np.save(OUT/'max_t_null.npy',max_null)\n    # Figure 1: participant variation in anatomical ROI.\n    fig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(6.2,4.0),constrained_layout=True)\n    jitter=np.random.default_rng(SEED+1).normal(0,.045,n)\n    ax.scatter(jitter,roi_sub,s=26,alpha=.72,color='#245b78',edgecolor='white',linewidth=.35,zorder=3)\n    ax.errorbar([0],[roi_mean],yerr=[[roi_mean-roi_ci[0]],[roi_ci[1]-roi_mean]],fmt='D',color='#b3432f',markersize=7,capsize=5,lw=2,zorder=4,label='Mean and 95% t CI')\n    ax.axhline(0,color='0.4',lw=1,ls='--'); ax.set_xlim(-.25,.25); ax.set_xticks([])\n    ax.set_ylabel('Gain-effect estimate (upstream normalized regressor units)')\n    ax.set_title('Participant estimates in independent vmPFC sphere (N=54)')\n    ax.legend(frameon=False,loc='best'); fig.savefig(FIG/'vmPFC_roi_estimates.png',dpi=180); plt.close(fig)\n    # Figure 2: only whole-brain FWE-significant positive voxels, displayed over MNI template.\n    mean_sig=np.zeros(ref.shape,dtype=np.float32); mean_sig[mask]=np.where(sig,mean,0)\n    stat_img=nib.Nifti1Image(mean_sig,ref.affine,ref.header)\n    display=plotting.plot_glass_brain(stat_img,display_mode='lyrz',threshold=1e-12,colorbar=True,\n          title='Positive gain effect: whole-brain max-t FWE p ≤ .05',plot_abs=False,\n          cmap='cold_hot',vmax=float(np.max(mean[sig])) if sig.any() else None,output_file=str(FIG/'wholebrain_fwe.png'))\n    display.close()\n    # machine readable permutation details\n    with open(OUT/'analysis_log.txt','w') as f:\n        f.write('Command: python analysis/group_analysis.py\\n')\n        f.write(f'Input: {len(paths)} source-listed participant cope maps; all checks passed.\\n')\n        f.write(f'Common support: {mask.sum()} voxels; vmPFC proxy overlap: {roi.sum()} voxels.\\n')\n        f.write(f'Permutation max-t: {N_PERM} random sign flips, seed {SEED}; positive one-sided.\\n')\n        f.write(f'Discoveries at FWE alpha .05: {sig.sum()}\\n')\n    print(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))\n\nif __name__=='__main__': main()\n===== input/participants.tsv\nparticipant_id\tgroup\tgender\tage\nsub-001\tequalIndifference\tM\t24\nsub-003\tequalIndifference\tF\t27\nsub-005\tequalIndifference\tM\t27\nsub-009\tequalIndifference\tM\t26\nsub-011\tequalIndifference\tM\t30\nsub-013\tequalIndifference\tM\t26\nsub-015\tequalIndifference\tF\t26\nsub-017\tequalIndifference\tF\t24\nsub-019\tequalIndifference\tM\t25\nsub-021\tequalIndifference\tF\t22\nsub-025\tequalIndifference\tM\t25\nsub-027\tequalIndifference\tF\t27\nsub-029\