cal/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/assessment.py:189:        return finish(\"partial\" if identical or close else \"unmet\", \"Some selected generated outputs did not reproduce.\")\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/assessment.py:190:    return finish(\"met\", \"All selected generated outputs were recreated within the frozen comparison tolerance.\")\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/assessment.py:195:    parser.add_argument(\"action\", choices=(\"check\", \"probes\", \"response\", \"validate\", \"fresh-rerun\"))\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/assessment.py:251:        helper = scripts / {\"probes\": \"run_probes.py\", \"fresh-rerun\": \"fresh_rerun.py\"}[args.action]\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/assessment.py:252:    if frozen and args.action == \"fresh-rerun\":\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/credit-contributions/CREDIT_ROLES.md:29:| 11 | Validation | `validation` | Verification, whether as a part of the activity or separate, of the overall replication/reproducibility of results/experiments and other research outputs. |\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/pixi-with-stamped/SKILL.md:18:Expose useful operations as named tasks with inputs, outputs and parameters appropriate to the work: analysis, figures, validation, replay or worker launch.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/pixi-with-stamped/SKILL.md:41:Retain command metadata, stdout/stderr, resource usage and the completed summary with outputs; annex large records.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/pixi-with-stamped/SKILL.md:43:Record environment and run identities so scientific outputs, execution records and replay receipts can be connected.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/introduce-codespell/SKILL.md:514:| `nbstripout` | yes | Strips notebook outputs |\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/datalad-annex/SKILL.md:16:Use native `datalad run --explicit` or `containers-run` with declared code, data, environment inputs and generated outputs.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/datalad-annex/SKILL.md:32:Inspect effective attributes before adding files; keep code and small specifications in Git and large outputs/records in annex.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:3:Every STAMPED assessment produces four files (five with the optional fresh-rerun report), named for **the day the assessment was made** (UTC, `YYYY-MM-DD`) — not the object's commit date, and not the date of an earlier assessment being redone:\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:11:| `<date>-fresh-rerun.json` | only when the expensive rerun probe was actually run |\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/review-org-code-quality/SKILL.md:75:- Extract the **house pattern**: directory layout, config approach, entrypoint shape, logging, retry/error handling, testing layout, how secrets are read, how schemas are declared, how outputs are written.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/PLAN.md:291:     Write the question, inputs, method and expected outputs into the project, and commit them.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/PLAN.md:306:     If aggregation turns up gaps or outliers, go back into the loop of step 3 rather than patching outputs.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/PLAN.md:423:  - R1–R3, then R4 as a demonstration with NIDM and BEP028 outputs.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/PLAN.md:601:**`fresh-rerun` ran for the first time** — §10.1 has always named it, and\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/PLAN.md:612:**all four outputs, the three tables and the annexed figure, came back\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/PLAN.md:629:  command whose outputs did not change exited 1 — the wrapper reporting\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/PLAN.md:773:    What is left for a **real** URL (and so for `met` and for the fresh-rerun probe to test published URLs, as [evals.md §9](evals.md#9-where-results-live) anticipates) is credentials inside the run, which is the part not to rush: a token with write access to a forge, handed to a blind agent that commits files, is a leak waiting to happen. The outer loop is where that belongs, with a per-run repository and a credential helper outside the sandbox.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/eval-platforms.md:34:| [**promptfoo**](https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/configuration/expected-outputs/) | one `promptfooconfig.yaml`, `promptfoo eval` | Ollama provider | no | no (JS/CLI) | Prompt-centric rather than object-centric. Worth borrowing its **`llm-rubric`** idea for grading \"did the report name the defect\" if substring matching proves brittle. |\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/eval-platforms.md:72:- [promptfoo assertions and metrics](https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/configuration/expected-outputs/)\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-repronim-stamped-project/SKILL.md:23:Deliver executable tasks, identities, useful outputs and a scoped assessment.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/evals.md:52:A run has a scope, a condition ([§4](#4-conditions)), a model, and a place its outputs go.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/evals.md:117:- *Oracle:* a deterministic rerun gives identical outputs.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/evals.md:262:| **`fresh-rerun`** | The documented rerun reproduces the outputs on another host (below) | A.1, P.1–3, E, D.1, should/004 |\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/evals.md:265:`fresh-rerun` in detail:\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/evals.md:269:4. Compare outputs: checksums, or a tolerance for plots and tables.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/evals.md:343:   The skill-creator viewer is available for browsing outputs.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/evals.md:371:  That way `subdatasets-resolvable` and `fresh-rerun` test real published URLs rather than paths on typhon.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/docs/stamped/evals.md:426:  - at R0–R2, explicit-skill runs — which are blind runs with a PROMPT as their scope — pass every mechanically checkable MUST probe, including `fresh-rerun`, in ≥ 2 of 3 repeats on two model tiers.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/do-full-research-loop/SKILL.md:31:1. Run the smallest useful unit through the project's recorded mechanism with explicit inputs and outputs.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/do-full-research-loop/SKILL.md:35:   Retain failed attempts and partial outputs separately from accepted results, with interventions and their reasons.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/do-full-research-loop/SKILL.md:57:Replay from a fresh checkout with generated outputs absent and the recorded environment restored.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/do-full-research-loop/references/validation.md:33:Remove only declared generated outputs, without deleting source data or shared annex content; keep expected artifacts elsewhere.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/do-full-research-loop/references/validation.md:42:Retrieve original outputs and requested logs separately when testing delivery; metadata availability does not prove payload retrieval.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-repronim-stamped-project/references/repronim.md:25:Use the project's DataLad `run`/`containers-run` mechanism with explicit inputs, outputs and environment identity.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-repronim-stamped-project/references/repronim.md:31:Replay declared generated outputs in a disposable checkout with those outputs absent; compare their content with a separate expected result.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/SKILL.md:19:1. Identify the research-object root, input identities and access terms, module boundaries, expected outputs and retrieval route.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/SKILL.md:28:   Keep reusable code and small specifications in Git; use annex for large inputs, outputs and requested logs.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/SKILL.md:29:4. Implement a runnable slice with declared inputs and outputs.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/SKILL.md:38:6. Write a short README: question, declared inputs, existing executable task, environment/replay route, outputs and observed limits.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles/SKILL.md:12:**Input:** a POINTER — a local path, a git/DataLad URL, or \"this project\" — and optionally a scope (\"only the derivatives\", \"skip the containers\"). **Output:** four files — `<date>-assessment.md`, `<date>-response.json`, `<date>-probes.json`, `<date>-url.txt` (the app URL, which is 8–10 kB and belongs in a file, not inlined in the report) — and `<date>-fresh-rerun.json` only if replay ran. **Boundary:** read the object, write only your own report files. Never commit to or fix the source object. Execute only an optional, authorized replay below; keep its copy separate. Fixing is [`align-with-stamped-principles`](../align-with-stamped-principles/); say so and stop.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles/SKILL.md:92:Before an authorized attempt, record the delivered command, exact source/snapshot, generated outputs, comparison method and scientifically justified tolerances; inspect selector expansion to exclude inputs, supplied resources and unrelated files. Use the helper only when its clone/materialization route and comparisons fit that plan:\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles/SKILL.md:95:python3 scripts/fresh_rerun.py --url <published url> --entry '<delivered command>' \\\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles/SKILL.md:96:    --outputs '<generated-output selection>' --rtol <justified tolerance> -o <date>-fresh-rerun.json\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles/SKILL.md:104:Matching outputs establish computational repeatability, not scientific validity; report scientific checks separately.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles/SKILL.md:201:  Preserve the delivered evidence boundary; assessor outputs are not worker artifacts and cannot change worker-practice verdicts.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/templates/run-recorded.sh:10:#       mri_synthstrip -i {inputs} -m {outputs}\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/templates/run-recorded.sh:16:# one record inside another and declares no inputs or outputs — found by an\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/templates/run-recorded.sh:34:# `datalad run` does not create the directories of its outputs. After a\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/templates/run-recorded.sh:179:# A command whose outputs do not change leaves nothing to commit, and\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/create-stamped-project/templates/pre-commit-run-guard:9:# --output\", and a workflow engine then deletes the *completed* outputs of that\n/Users/jo