{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba assessment-report.md | sed -n '20,34p'\"","aggregated_output":"    20\t\n    21\t- The scientific analysis is transparent and unusually well specified: it uses the full 54-person cohort, checks hashes and spatial geometry, defines common support, and performs positive one-sided max-t sign-flip inference over the whole analysis mask. The vmPFC sphere is defined independently and the ROI result is kept descriptive. (Capture citation: `content/workspace/protocol.md`, `content/workspace/analysis/group_analysis.py`, `content/workspace/results/summary.json`.)\n    22\t- The report correctly interprets the negative vmPFC estimate as no support for the hypothesized positive response, not proof of a zero effect; it explains normalized-regressor units and missing first-level variance maps. The figures, QC table, code and machine-readable summary are present in the stop-state delivery. (Capture citation: `content/workspace/report/analysis-report.md`, `content/workspace/figures/`, `content/workspace/results/`.)\n    23\t- Large inputs were annexed and materialized in the captured workspace, and the worker recorded checksums and a replay history. The frozen assessment replay on a separate complete copy also recreated all 12 declared outputs byte-for-byte. The latter is assessor measurement, not worker-practice credit. (Capture citation: `content/workspace/.git/annex/`, `content/workspace/input/sources.json`, `content/workspace/results/run_history.md`; evaluator record: `replay/replay.json`.)\n    24\t\n    25\t## Scientific judgment\n    26\t\n    27\t**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The supplied analysis provides a defensible test of the positive vmPFC hypothesis using the supplied fixed upstream maps. It uses the independent participant as the sampling unit; verifies all 54 source-listed maps, metadata joins, finite values, shared image shape and affine; and restricts inference to finite nonzero common coverage so zero-filled outside-mask voxels are not treated as observations. The group mean is tested with a one-sided sign-flip max-t procedure over 198,029 voxels, which addresses the required whole-brain correction. Its sign-exchangeability assumption is stated, the seed and plus-one p-value are recorded, and a SciPy check supports the statistic implementation. The 5 mm MNI sphere at [2, 46, -8] is an explicit independent anatomical proxy rather than a post hoc peak; the report does not use its uncorrected p-value as the primary decision.\n    28\t\n    29\tThe reported outcome is no support for a greater vmPFC response: the sphere mean is −0.012 upstream normalized-regressor units, its 95% t interval includes zero, and there is no positive whole-brain corrected discovery inside the sphere. Positive corrected voxels occur posteriorly, not in the defined vmPFC region. This is a careful absence-of-support conclusion, not a claim of no effect. The analysis also properly limits interpretation because coefficients are not per-currency-unit slopes, gain and loss were modeled separately upstream, and first-level variance maps are unavailable. The result is conditional on AO86's supplied participant models and on the sign-flip assumptions; it does not test gain against loss or establish causality.\n    30\t\n    31\t**Scientific conclusion:** “The supplied group maps do not support a greater vmPFC response with increasing potential gain.” This is the report's conclusion, retained separately from the adequacy label.\n    32\t\n    33\t## Replay measurement\n    34\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport hashlib,json,os,stat\nfrom pathlib import Path\nm=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_OPERATIONAL_MANIFEST']))\nbase=Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET']).parents[1]\nexpected={e['path']:e for e in m['entries']}\nactual=set()\nfor root,dirs,files in os.walk(base,followlinks=False):\n    rp=Path(root)\n    for name in list(dirs):\n        p=rp/name; rel=p.relative_to(base).as_posix(); actual.add(rel)\n        if p.is_symlink(): dirs.remove(name)\n    for name in files:\n        actual.add((rp/name).relative_to(base).as_posix())\ndef sha(b): return hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()\ndiffs=[]\nfor rel,e in expected.items():\n p=base/rel\n if not p.exists() and not p.is_symlink(): diffs.append({'path':rel,'difference':'missing'}); continue\n st=p.lstat(); mode=stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode)\n if e['kind']=='directory':\n  if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) or mode\"'!=e['\"'mode']: diffs.append({'path':rel,'difference':'directory-type-or-mode','expected_mode':e['mode'],'actual_mode':mode})\n elif e['kind']=='symlink':\n  target=os.readlink(p)\n  if target\"'!=e.get('\"'link_target'): diffs.append({'path':rel,'difference':'symlink-target','expected':e.get('link_target'),'actual':target})\n elif e['kind']=='file':\n  if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode): diffs.append({'path':rel,'difference':'file-type'}); continue\n  h=hashlib.sha256()\n  with open(p,'rb') as f:\n   for b in iter(lambda:f.read(1024*1024),b''): h.update(b)\n  actualhash=h.hexdigest()\n  if actualhash\"'!=e.get('\"'sha256') or mode\"'!=e.get('\"'mode'):\n   allowed=rel in {'content/workspace/.git/annex/keysdb/db','content/workspace/.git/annex/keysdb/db-shm','content/workspace/.git/annex/keysdb/db-wal'}\n   diffs.append({'path':rel,'difference':'bytes-or-mode','expected_sha256':e.get('sha256'),'actual_sha256':actualhash,'expected_mode':e.get('mode'),'actual_mode':mode,'classification':'allowed-operational-metadata-only' if allowed else 'integrity-mismatch'})\nfor rel in sorted(actual-set(expected)):\n if rel=='manifest.json': continue\n allowed=rel in {'content/workspace/.git/annex/keysdb/db-shm','content/workspace/.git/annex/keysdb/db-wal'}\n diffs.append({'path':rel,'difference':'added','classification':'allowed-operational-metadata-only' if allowed else 'integrity-mismatch'})\nresult={'canonical_capture_sha256':m.get('capture_sha256',json.load(open('judge-target.json'))['capture']['sha256']),'operational_manifest_sha256':os.popen('shasum -a 256 '+os.environ['STAMPED_OPERATIONAL_MANIFEST']).read().split()[0], 'expected_entries':len(expected),'differences':diffs,'integrity_mismatch_count':sum(d.get('classification')\"'!='\"'allowed-operational-metadata-only' for d in diffs),'operational_metadata_difference_count':sum(d.get('classification')=='allowed-operational-metadata-only' for d in diffs),'logical_database_equivalence_established':False}\nopen('integrity-check.json','w').write(json.dumps(result,indent=2)+'\\\\n'); print(json.dumps(result,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
