{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'SHOULD:|should/001|Capture verification|manifest comparison|extra item|Scientific adequacy|The supplied group maps' assessment-report.md\"","aggregated_output":"7:SHOULD: 0 met / 2 partial / 6 unmet / 0 not-checked / 1 not-applicable (9 total).\n14:2. Track the analysis code, report, protocol, figures and generated results at the worker stop → these are the core scientific deliverables, but they were untracked in the captured state → must/004; should/001.\n27:**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The supplied analysis provides a defensible test of the positive vmPFC hypothesis using the supplied fixed upstream maps. It uses the independent participant as the sampling unit; verifies all 54 source-listed maps, metadata joins, finite values, shared image shape and affine; and restricts inference to finite nonzero common coverage so zero-filled outside-mask voxels are not treated as observations. The group mean is tested with a one-sided sign-flip max-t procedure over 198,029 voxels, which addresses the required whole-brain correction. Its sign-exchangeability assumption is stated, the seed and plus-one p-value are recorded, and a SciPy check supports the statistic implementation. The 5 mm MNI sphere at [2, 46, -8] is an explicit independent anatomical proxy rather than a post hoc peak; the report does not use its uncorrected p-value as the primary decision.\n31:**Scientific conclusion:** “The supplied group maps do not support a greater vmPFC response with increasing potential gain.” This is the report's conclusion, retained separately from the adequacy label.\n68:| should/001 | T.2 | met | `.git/`, `.git/annex/`: one Git repository with annex storage covers the delivered root and large inputs, though key scientific materials remained untracked. |\n85:`entry-point` marked must/007 and must/008 unmet. Reading the delivered README and script supports a partial must/007 and met must/008: the entrypoint is clearly named, although its invocation depends on a host-specific interpreter and has no setup guidance. These two responses are flagged `probe-overridden` in `response.json`. Other probe findings are retained in `probes.json`. The license probe also found no declared project license; this is recorded as an extra item in `response.json`. No checklist item remains not-checked; the absence of documented environments/remotes was assessable from the complete captured root and worker stop-state files.\n93:Assessment runtime: frozen `assessment.py` source commit `9852d8360f9519d21d11099b45f5deb8ba80cb28`, environment commit `3552d5003a2485b6405805236d5c54e7ed42f097`; runner check passed before probe, replay and response actions. The operational copy was used for inspection and Git commands. The operational manifest comparison found no invalidating mismatches; `.git/annex/keysdb/db` changed during inspection and is classified only as allowed operational metadata. Logical database equivalence is not established (`integrity-check.json`). The worker stop receipt SHA-256 is `032361148ea1f213f1360b9ab2eb408288dc978cae37befebf9527c1169130a2`. No coordinator-only preservation action is credited to the worker.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
